  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>r</mi></math> be the three statements such that<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>r</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br />Here given statement is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>r</mi></math> and its contrapositive is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />i.e. <math><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />i.e. if <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>9</mn></math> then <math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>6</mn></math> or <math><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>"
